tortoise-wow: VMaNGOS Eluna gets the TrinityCore script API that scripts port with.

Added to the VMaNGOS backend (methods/VMangos, hooks, LuaValue):
- Global GetStateMap() (map states only) and GetPlayersOnMap([team, onlyGM])
  (the players of the state's own map, the map-state replacement for
  GetPlayersInWorld). GetStateMapId / GetStateInstanceId are left to 0011.
- RegisterSpellEvent(entry, event, fn[, shots]) for the events the core fires:
  1 cast, 10 check cast, 11 before cast, 12 after cast, 19 effect hit,
  20 before hit, 21 effect hit target, 22 hit, 23 after hit. Any other event is
  an argument error (it would never fire). The hit unit is passed as a trailing
  argument of the hit events (Spell::unitTarget is protected). A check-cast
  result that is a SPELL_FAILED_* value cancels the cast; SPELL_CAST_OK lets it
  go on, and a value outside both counts as OK. The check-cast handler is called
  as (event, spell, strict) on every CheckCast: strict is true at prepare and
  false at the completion check.
- Creature:GetThreat, ClearThreat, ResetAllThreat, FixateTarget, ClearFixate
  (the fixate is emulated by the core through the taunt target).
  ClearThreat removes the unit's reference through the target's HostileRefManager, so it
  leaves the online and the offline container.
- Spell:IsTriggered, GetOriginalCaster, IsPositive, GetState, IsInterruptable,
  IsChannelActive, CalculateDamage.
- WorldObject:Data() and Map:Data() (the LuaVal the core already stores). A
  LuaVal given to Set/AsLuaVal is now deep-copied (value semantics), so two
  objects never share one map across threads and a table cannot contain itself; nesting deeper than 64 levels (a plain table that holds itself too) is refused with an error, never cut.
- ChatHandler type: the third argument of PLAYER_EVENT_ON_COMMAND (new overload
  Eluna::OnCommand(ChatHandler&, text)) with SendSysMessage, PSendSysMessage,
  IsConsole, GetPlayer, GetAccountId, GetSecurity, IsAvailable,
  HasLowerSecurity, GetSelected*, SendGlobal(GM)SysMessage and the error flag.
  World-only methods; the new file methods/VMangos/ChatHandlerMethods.h.

Partly upstreamable: the LuaVal value semantics and RegisterSpellEvent are not
VMaNGOS-specific; the hit unit argument and the ChatHandler are.

Base: ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna 1b06f28ff3a00054d915d824c725fb4283fee74d (branch
cmangos-spell-update), the dep/Eluna pin, with patches 0001-0011 applied. Eluna is
GPL-3.0 (https://github.com/ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna, LICENSE); this change is under
the same licence. Applied by cmake/ElunaSources.cmake to a copy in the build tree.
